Description: Native haptics and Actions Ring for the Logitech MX Master 4
 mx-master-4-desktop adds native HID++ haptic feedback and an on-demand
 "Actions Ring" radial menu overlay for the Logitech MX Master 4 mouse on
 Linux desktops (Plasma 6 Wayland, LXQt, and other X11/Wayland environments).
 .
 It ships three components:
  * mx4d   - a Python daemon (run on the system python, no venv/pip) that
             talks raw HID++ to the mouse, drives the haptic engine, and
             diverts the Actions Ring button to show the overlay;
  * mx4-radial - a Qt6/QML radial-menu overlay (Wayland layer-shell when
             available, X11 otherwise), lazy-launched by the daemon;
  * mx4-config - a Qt6/QML settings GUI for haptics, ambient sources and the
             radial menu.
 .
 Small shell helpers are also installed: mx4-show (ask the daemon to open the
 ring over D-Bus, bindable to any hotkey) and mx4-playpause (toggle play/pause
 on the active MPRIS player via qdbus6 with a dbus-send fallback, no playerctl).
 .
 The package is init-agnostic: it ships a portable XDG autostart entry that
 starts the daemon on any init (systemd, OpenRC, runit, s6) and additionally
 provides systemd user units. A Plasma-Wayland KWin focus-bridge script is
 shipped as data (never enabled, never pulls Plasma as a hard dependency).
